From e2b042a909d783ed0555083d71eb360a8cdc8d80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:45:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] Round 2: Prepare the SIR projection once and bind rates
 per candidate

Build the reachable SIR states, generator edges and column order once at
preparation (src/sir_fsp.rs) after CRN-craft accepts the model and run
documents. Each untraced, unmonitored candidate with positive normal rates
binds its two rates to that structure and runs the vendored solver's
uniformization arithmetic in the same order, so means, diagnostics and
FSP work are bit-identical. Traced candidates, deadlines, cancel files and
every other condition fall back to crn_craft::fsp::solve. Full records
still build the CRN documents to report their SHA-256 values. Tests compare
the prepared path with the vendored solver bit for bit over 430 bindings
and compare whole records against the forced reference path.
validation/validate.py passed against the release CLI.

Workload: serial (96 SIR candidates, one worker), matrix API on both
sides, 11 samples.
Before median: 16.029 ms. After median: 2.212 ms. Speedup: 7.25x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
